+  "problem": "🔎 **REV (BARCHI-2, on my own surface)** — the WP-2026-0109 family-name guard passes vacuously when the surface it scans is absent\n\nFiled against myself, applying BARCHI-3's checklist from #221 — *\"for each guard, ask what it does when its input is missing; if the answer is 'passes', it is not a guard\"* — to the guard I shipped two work packages ago.\n\n## Measured (detached probe at `origin/main` `ce3c458`, restored)\n`tests/test_badf_build_contract.py::test_every_family_named_in_the_surface_resolves_in_the_registry` collects `badf-*` tokens by `(ROOT / \"skills\" / \"badf-build\").rglob(\"*.md\")` and asserts none are unresolved. With `skills/badf-build/` moved aside:\n\n```\nRan 1 test in 0.000s\nOK          ← surface absent; guard passes\n```\n\nrestored → `OK` again (0.002s). **Absence of the surface is indistinguishable from a clean surface.** The guard's own defect (`badf-verification` unresolved) would also vanish under a rename: the check would go quiet exactly when the thing it protects stopped existing.\n\nThis is instance ten of the class and the second one **introduced while remediating** — BADF-REV's M2 (`if live.is_file()` silently vacuous) was the ninth, in the fix for the eighth. My guard was written to close a naming defect and shipped with the same hole in a different shape: `is_file()` standing for \"there is something to check\" there, an empty glob standing for it here.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- The guard asserts it actually scanned the surface before concluding: at minimum `SKILL.md` plus the fourteen `references/*.md` were read, and the token set contains `badf-build` itself (the surface cannot describe itself without naming itself).\n- Red-verified by moving the surface aside — the probe above must fail, not pass — and restored byte-identical.\n- Same question asked of the sibling `badf-build` guards while there: `test_badf_build_shadow` and `test_badf_build_evidence` carry anti-vacuity thresholds (4 each); `test_badf_build_activation` and `test_badf_build_controls` iterate literal tuples and fixture globs used for cleanup, not assertions — measured, no change needed. Stated so the next reader need not re-derive it.\n- No change to `badf_gate.py`, schemas, or any other family's surface.\n\n## Not in scope\nGeneralizing to other families' surfaces — that is #223's territory, and BADF-REV documented the trap there (`badf-security-assurance` is unresolved in ten places *correctly*, \"named, not built\"), so a naive generalization would flag deliberate forward references.\n\n**Version tier:** patch. Ids: `GOV-0099` claimed here; the WP/DEM pair will be measured **and asked for** at filing time — GOV is safely measurable alone because issue titles are a complete surface, unlike WP/DEM ids which can exist in an unpushed tree (#227).\n\n<!-- agent: reviewer -->\n",
